.TH wo 8 "WordOps 3.22.0" "2026-03-04" "WordOps"
.SH NAME
wo \- manage Nginx-based website and server operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wo
[--version] [--help] <command> [subcommand] [options]

.SH DESCRIPTION
WordOps is a CLI for provisioning and operating websites and server components.
The current implementation supports static, PHP, MySQL, proxy, alias, and WordPress site workflows,
plus stack/package management and maintenance tools.

.SH TOP-LEVEL COMMANDS
.TP
.B site
Website lifecycle operations (create/update/delete/backup/restore/secure/autoupdate).
.TP
.B stack
Install/upgrade/remove/purge/migrate components and manage services.
.TP
.B log
Show/reset/gzip/mail logs.
.TP
.B info
Display nginx/php/mysql configuration summaries.
.TP
.B clean
Clean fastcgi/opcache/redis caches.
.TP
.B secure
Security operations (SSH hardening via
.BR "wo secure ssh" .
.TP
.B debug
Enable/disable debug settings and slow-log import helpers.
.TP
.B maintenance
Run apt update/dist-upgrade/autoclean/autoremove.
.TP
.B sync
Sync site database records with on-disk config files.
.TP
.B update
WordOps self-update command (alias of internal
.B wo_update
controller).
.TP
.B import_slow_log
Deprecated shim; use
.B wo debug --import-slow-log
instead.

.SH SITE COMMANDS
.TP
.B wo site create <domain> [options]
Create site types:
.B --html --php --mysql --wp --wpsubdir --wpsubdomain --proxy --alias
with optional PHP version selectors
.B --php74 .. --php84
and SSL options
.B -le/--letsencrypt
.
.TP
.B wo site update <domain> [options]
Transition site/cache/php version, SSL/HSTS, nginx blocker, etc.
.TP
.B wo site delete <domain> [--db] [--files] [--all] [--force] [--no-prompt]
Delete site config and optional data.
.TP
.B wo site backup <domain>|--all [--db] [--files] [--path DIR]
Create backup archive.
.TP
.B wo site restore <backup_path>
Restore site from backup archive/directory containing
.B vhost.json
.
.TP
.B wo site clone <source_domain> <dest_domain> [--user] [--email] [--pass]
Clone an existing WordPress site (WordPress-only flow; non-WordPress sources are rejected).
.TP
.B wo site secure <domain> [<user> <pass>] [--rm]
Manage per-site HTTP basic authentication.
.TP
.B wo site autoupdate run [<domain>|--all] [--dry-run] [--no-visual] [--backup-dir DIR]
Run WordPress update pipeline with backup and rollback (WordPress sites only).
.TP
.B wo site autoupdate schedule --enable|--disable [--interval=hourly|daily]
Install or remove autoupdate systemd timer.
.TP
.B wo site autoupdate backstop [<domain>|--all] [--urls CSV] [--urls-file FILE] [--reference] [--approve]
Configure BackstopJS visual regression hook.

.SH STACK COMMANDS
.TP
.B wo stack install [options]
Install selected components.
.TP
.B wo stack remove [options]
Remove selected components.
.TP
.B wo stack purge [options]
Purge selected components.
.TP
.B wo stack upgrade [options]
Upgrade selected components.
.TP
.B wo stack migrate [--mariadb] [--nginx] [--force]
Migration helpers.
.TP
.B wo stack start|stop|restart|reload|status [options]
Manage stack services.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/wo/wo.conf
Main WordOps configuration.
.TP
.B /etc/wo/plugins.d/
Plugin configuration files.
.TP
.B /var/lib/wo/dbase.db
Site metadata SQLite DB (default path in code).
.TP
.B /var/log/wo/wordops.log
WordOps log file.

.SH NOTES
All commands require root privileges.
wo site restore is generic, but proxy/alias backups may restore with partial fidelity because upstream/alias target details are not fully reconstructed from metadata.

.SH BUGS
Report issues at:
https://github.com/WordOps/WordOps/issues
